# Real Rails Example
Important Bigger Realization - Rails models are basically: advanced Ruby classes with built-in database powers.
With Rails - “Objects are connected to database records automatically.”
- Rails created a built-in parent/base class called: APPLICATIONRECORD (a built-in Rails CLASS) - It already knows how to: talk to database, save records, update records, delete records, run queries - inherits tons of functionality from Rails.
That's the difference between a class you create Ex. class Person (only knows what you teach it) vs. Rails class Ex. class User < ApplicationRecord (inherits tons of functionality from Rails like - It already knows how to: talk to database, save records, update records, delete records, run queries)

Abstraction - means hiding complicated details and giving you a simpler way to use something - Ex. Driving, you press gas, steer - but you do not need to know about engine combustion, etc.
Functionality - means features/behaviors a system provides Ex. - word.upcase has functionality; it converts text to uppercase

In Rails:

```ruby id="jlwm1k"
class User < ApplicationRecord
```

or:

```ruby id="jlwm5n"
class Job < ApplicationRecord
```

These are classes.

Your database records become objects created from classes.

