# What `initialize` Means

You wrote:

```ruby id="xmlns8"
def initialize(name, artist, duration)
```

`initialize` is a special Ruby method. & IS REQUERIED to define your method in you class so it can automatically recieve/setup data when a new object is created and calls the class.

It automatically runs when you do:

```ruby id="xmlns9"
Song.new(...)
```

It sets up the object’s starting data.

