# Important Bigger Concept

Classes teach:

* object-oriented programming - a programming style that organizes code around objects/classes that contain both data (state) and behavior (methods/functionality)
* abstraction - hiding complicated internal details and exposing only what is neccessary to use something 
* organization - structuring code/data clean, understandable, and manageable way
* modular design - breaking software into smaller reusable pieces/modules with focused responsibilities
* scalable architecture - designing software so it can continue working efficiently as users, data, and features grow

This is one of the major foundations of backend engineering.

